s-agc6fb3vx46pc23.text:
`sheriff validate` rebuilds these in memory and compares them with what is committed:

- the index of each domain's header, the header read as it now stands in the domain's files;
- the incoming links;
- the values gathered beside each field (§s-ju5vcanbjph7mgh);
- the status of each section and domain's header (§s-9kfdycuq34beqvs).

s-qvgzubkrafadqgf.text:
`sheriff validate` reads what stands at each end of every `consumes` and `exempts` link:

- a `consumes` link, for a domain's header at its start and a section of another domain at its end;
- an `exempts` link, for a node of `project.json` at its start, and a rule, a node of a project's own NodeKind or a section at its end.

s-c2r9jndrjbtbsv6.text:
`sheriff validate` checks that each RecordType variant agrees with the RecordType it refines, found by the variant's `refines` link:

- the fields the variant answers to are those the nearest RecordType up its `refines` links names as choosing it;
- each value it answers to is among the values of its choosing field, collected from the field's one source (§s-5nf87c3e3jg9v7c);
- the variant stands in the part of the specification where its value is declared (§s-xfwuvd3funutmsw);
- the variant declares at least one field that no RecordType up its `refines` links holds, the fields their fields of type `variant` hold included;
- at most one field of type `variant` stands along those links;
- no other variant of the same RecordType answers to the same values.

A variant failing any of these is refused.

s-5nf87c3e3jg9v7c.text:
`sheriff validate` collects the values of each field of type `one of` from its one source (§s-xfu2gpzddjnmgks), which is one of these:

- its own list;
- the members of each `TextRule.list` a rule of a domain adds to it. Each such list is found through its rule's `refines` link, which leads to the RecordType of contracts holding the field. The list names that field (§s-gzfq3x8hesj227e);
- the names of the domains;
- the sids of the nodes of the NodeKind it names that stand in the base specification.

It refuses:

- a field holding no value;
- a value found in two lists that rules of domains add to the field;
- a domain's list whose rule refines no RecordType of contracts;
- a domain's list naming a field the RecordType its rule refines does not hold;
- a domain's list naming a field whose source is another;
- a NodeKind named that the schema does not hold.

s-6bmnsbskg6en4nf.text:
`sheriff validate` refuses a copy of the SpecSheriff guidelines or of their schema outside the repository they are written in. A copy is:

- a `spec.json` or a `tools.json` under `specs/_guidelines/`;
- any file under `specs/_schema/` but `project.schema.json`.

s-dbk2vyeg8z5jxna.text:
`sheriff binding` generates in memory the copies the nodes produce, and compares them with what is committed. The copies are:

- the files the technical appendix lists for the types and RuntimeChecks (§s-pvzms7d8kxb8dk2);
- the files each of the project's own generators prints, run as `sheriff types` runs it (§s-km4x4s26kv7pjze).

Each copy is compared with what the last commit holds instead while a node it waits for is a draft (§s-f5rz6b7dhxejjts). Each such node is reported.

It refuses:

- a list of the files for the types and RuntimeChecks naming a file of another extension or a path outside the repository;
- a path a project's generator prints outside the repository or under `specs/`;
- two rules of the stack each defining such a list;
- a name that cannot be generated (§s-suv42g8r3ra2h6b);
- a RecordType holding two fields of type `variant`, its inherited ones counted.

s-txbwsthdqhvyzd2.text:
`sheriff binding` reports a node whose tests or code lag behind it, by the order rule, test, code.

The check takes the references to the files from the node's `meta.code` and `meta.tests` (§s-t383grkn3q68dpf). It learns from the history of the repository when each of those files and the node's text last changed. The history is read as follows:

- changes made in one commit count as made at once;
- a commit whose only change to a file of tests puts `@spec ` before bare sids (§s-rah8b37kytb682y) does not count as changing that file;
- a renamed file is followed under its earlier names too.

It reports the node where:

- its text changed later than every file of its tests: the tests lag;
- its text changed later than every file of its code: the code lags;
- its tests changed later than every file of its code: the code may not have caught up with the tests.

The node is reported by its sid, naming what lags. The change is not refused.

s-qqs2svksmjct753.text:
A commit that changes code names in its message, by sid, every node the SpecTags on its changed symbols outside the tests name. `sheriff message` refuses the message where:

- a node a SpecTag on a changed symbol outside the tests names is not named in it;
- a sid in it names no node;
- a sid in it names a domain's header or a section, which no code implements.

s-vp24dqydygztqbt.text:
`sheriff review` has a runner judge every commit that changes the system's code. A runner is an agent's CLI, started apart from the session that wrote the code (§s-xr5xxa9cxf2mq5u). The runner is given:

- the commit's message;
- the commit's change, less the files generated from the nodes, each of which is named to it with what it holds;
- each node the message or a changed symbol's SpecTag names, with its text and its reason. A RecordType is given with its `RecordType.fields`, and a node of a project's own NodeKind with the values its NodeKind declares;
- each symbol of the system's code outside its tests the commit changes, whole as the commit leaves it, with its file, its lines and its SpecTags.

The symbols are those `sheriff binding` finds changed (§s-2x58az67bm6cxq2). A symbol's SpecTags are its own or those of the symbol it stands in.

The runner judges the commit against the nodes. It judges each changed symbol, whole, against the nodes its SpecTags name.

It refuses the commit where the code:

- does something no named node states in its text;
- leaves out what a named node requires.

It also refuses the commit where a changed symbol:

- does something no node its SpecTags name states in its text;
- carries a SpecTag naming a node it does not implement;
- carries the SpecTag that names no node while it implements the system's logic.

A finding of the last sort names as its node the rule that every symbol carries a SpecTag (§s-kgbzk2ph9e6jfb4).
